# Front-end only. The deployment is the contents of public/ and nothing else.
#
# api/ is excluded deliberately: Vercel turns any .py file in that folder into
# a serverless function, and a function is precisely what this deployment is
# meant not to have. Nothing here can crash, because nothing here runs.
#
# To put the working application back, delete this file's `api/` and `app/`
# lines and restore the function config in vercel.json — see git history for
# commit 3948954, which has both.

api/
app/
scripts/
tests/

# --- never publish: third-party business records ---
data/
Invoices/
samples/
.env
*.pdf

# --- not part of a static site ---
.venv/
.DS_Store
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
requirements.txt
requirements-training.txt
render.yaml
deploy-vercel.sh
README.md
EXTRACTION_PLAN.md
DEPLOY-VERCEL.md
run.sh
.gitignore
